                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Played On: [b]HTC Vive[/b][/h1]\n\nYou may have already guessed from the title that Smash Party is a game about smashing stuff; pure and simple, it's based off Titmouse's event, after all. You're in a small enclosure, you grab a bat, and you just start wailing away on cups, plates, vases, televisions, toilets, and shelves. If you hold your bat up to the sky (or over your head at least), the doob-smoking moon transforms your weapon into a powerful axe, and you can unleash a devastating blow for one hit before having to do it again. There's a catch though, you're on a time limit.\n\nThe art direction is absolutely incredible for anyone that loves the work of Ed Roth; the dude behind RatFink and multiple other psychedelic cartoon drawings. He's also the one that animated the music video in Beavis and Butthead Do America. Everything is done in bright, neon colors, all while a thundering metal instrumental is playing in the background. It sets the perfect tone for violent, mayhem-driven destruction, and it's all incredibly immersive. You'll definitely need to be careful as you're flailing about, especially if you barely meet the minimum 2mx1.5m room-scale requirement; my 2mx2m space didn't feel big enough.\n\nWithout a doubt, Smash Party is the most fun that I've had within a 6 minute time span on a free game in VR. It used up a lot of my energy, and got a lot of my anger out in just two short rounds. It's too bad that the developer, Viacom NEXT, have seemingly abandoned the project. Their last update only added global leaderboards, and that was in January of 2017. More objects, arenas, weapons, and modes would be a welcome addition, and more content overall could turn this small free game in to a profitable $10 CAD or less title. Either way, Smash Party is the best destructive VR game to date, you should check it out if you want to relieve some stress.\n\n[h1]Rating: [b]5.0/5.0[/b] - An astonishing achievement, this game must be played.[/h1]\nThe VR Network [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/33182845-The-VR-Network/]Curator[/url] | [url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/thevrnetwork]Group[/url] Click for More",
